.TH TAU 1 "August 2026" "tau 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tau \- High-performance, pure Rust autonomous coding agent and swarm orchestrator (2π Evolution of Pi)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tau
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B tau
\fB\-\-print\fR \fI"QUERY"\fR [\fB\-\-model\fR \fIMODEL_ID\fR]
.br
.B tau
\fB\-\-rpc\fR
.br
.B tau
\fB\-\-replay\fR \fIPATH_TO_SESSION.jsonl\fR [\fB\-\-replay-delay-ms\fR \fIMS\fR]
.br
.B tau
\fB\-\-login\fR [\fIPROVIDER\fR]
.br
.B tau
\fB\-\-models\fR | \fB\-\-refresh-models\fR
.br
.B tau
\fB\-\-completions\fR \fISHELL\fR
.br
.B tau
\fB\-\-init\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tau
is a 100% pure Rust autonomous agentic coding engine representing the 2π evolution of Mario Zechner's Pi Coding Agent (\fBpi.dev\fR / \fBearendil-works/pi\fR).
Engineered for speed, safety, and zero external runtime dependencies (zero Node.js/V8/npm), \fBtau\fR provides an interactive terminal user interface (TUI) powered by Ratatui with 7 visual themes, an asynchronous dual-protocol tool execution engine, a bi-directional JSON-RPC 2.0 server daemon for IDE integrations (Neovim/VSCode), and multi-agent swarm orchestration with First Mate and Herdr protocols.

\fBtau\fR operates against a directed acyclic graph (DAG) session tree, allowing arbitrary branch rewinds, simulated rollback previews, branch visual diffs, and context window compaction when token usage approaches model context limits.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-print " \fIQUERY\fR"
Run in one-shot CLI print mode. Executes the user's query against the configured model, emits agent events, prints the final response to standard output, and exits cleanly.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-model " \fIMODEL_ID\fR"
Specify the AI model identifier to use (e.g. \fIopencode/deepseek-v4-flash-free\fR, \fIanthropic/claude-3-7-sonnet-latest\fR, \fIopenai/gpt-4o\fR, \fIkilo/deepseek-r1\fR, \fIollama/llama3\fR). Defaults to \fIopencode/deepseek-v4-flash-free\fR or value in \fI~/.pi/config.json\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-rpc
Launch \fBtau\fR in bidirectional JSON-RPC 2.0 daemon mode over standard input and standard output. Stdout is reserved exclusively for JSON-RPC messages and notifications; all operational logging is routed to stderr.
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-models
Query local cache and display a formatted table of all discovered and configured AI models across 35+ LLM providers, including context window sizes and reasoning/vision capabilities.
.TP
.B \-\-refresh-models
Force refresh online provider endpoints and local daemons (Ollama, LM Studio, vLLM, Kilo), update the catalog cache in \fI~/.pi/agent/models.json\fR, and display available models.
.TP
.BR \-\-login " [\fIPROVIDER\fR]"
Interactive credential wizard to configure API tokens for cloud frontier providers (\fIanthropic\fR, \fIopenai\fR, \fIgemini\fR, \fIkilo\fR, \fIopenrouter\fR, \fIdeepseek\fR, \fIgroq\fR, etc.). Credentials are persisted securely to \fI~/.pi/config.json\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-replay " \fIPATH\fR"
Replay a stored JSONL session trajectory to stdout with step-by-step metadata, tool call traces, and token metrics.
.TP
.BR \-\-replay-delay-ms " \fIMS\fR"
Pacing delay in milliseconds between steps during session replay (default: 50ms).
.TP
.BR \-\-completions " \fISHELL\fR"
Generate shell auto-completion scripts to standard output. Supported shells: \fIbash\fR, \fIzsh\fR, \fIfish\fR, \fIpowershell\fR, \fIelvish\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-init
Run the interactive first-run onboarding setup wizard: probes local daemons, tests provider connectivity, and saves preferences to \fI~/.pi/config.json\fR.
.TP
.B \-V\fR, \fB\-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \fB\-\-help
Print concise command-line help message and exit.

.SH INTERACTIVE TUI SHORTCUTS
Inside the interactive Cockpit TUI (\fBtau\fR without arguments):
.TP
.B Ctrl+L
Open live fuzzy Model Picker overlay with reasoning and vision badges.
.TP
.B Ctrl+P
Open Provider Picker overlay to filter by cloud or local provider.
.TP
.B Ctrl+T
Open Theme Picker overlay (Default Pi, Tokyo Night, Catppuccin, Gruvbox, Nord, Solarized, One Dark).
.TP
.B Ctrl+R
Trigger non-blocking background model catalog discovery and daemon refresh.
.TP
.B Ctrl+N
Start a clean, fresh agent session DAG.
.TP
.B Ctrl+O
Toggle tool execution drawer expansion.
.TP
.B ? \fRor\fB F1
Open interactive, searchable Help & Keymap Cheatsheet overlay.
.TP
.B Esc \fRor\fB Ctrl+C
Interrupt active model turn generation or dismiss open overlays.

.SH SLASH COMMANDS
.TP
.B /help
Display the interactive keyboard and command reference overlay.
.TP
.B /diff [file]
Compute and display unified terminal diff visualizer comparing proposed edits against git repository or working tree.
.TP
.B /theme [name]
Switch visual color theme palette in real-time.
.TP
.B /tree
Open the interactive DAG session tree navigator to branch and rewind history.
.TP
.B /models
List and filter configured AI models.
.TP
.B /skills
Inspect discovered autonomous agent skills in \fI.pi/skills/\fR and \fI~/.pi/agent/skills/\fR.
.TP
.B /mcp
List connected Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers and dynamic tools.
.TP
.B /login [provider]
Launch the in-TUI authentication credential wizard.
.TP
.B /session
Display session ID, active turn node count, token budget gauge, and capacity percentage.
.TP
.B /compact
Manually trigger context window history compaction.
.TP
.B /clear
Clear the visible transcript display buffer.
.TP
.B /quit\fR, \fB/exit
Exit the application cleanly.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.tau/bin/tau
Primary executable binary location.
.TP
.I ~/.pi/config.json
Primary configuration storing default models, custom providers, and API keys.
.TP
.I ~/.pi/agent/models.json
User-defined custom model catalogs and parameter overrides.
.TP
.I ~/.pi/agent/sessions/
Session DAG history trees persisted in line-delimited JSONL format.
.TP
.I .pi/worktrees/
Ephemeral Git worktree workspaces allocated for isolated swarm tasks.
.TP
.I AGENTS.md
Authoritative repository instructions and invariants loaded automatically by the agent engine.

